# api/Dockerfile.dockerignore
# Excludes for the repository-root build context. BuildKit reads
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context root's
# .dockerignore, which keeps this file next to the Dockerfile it serves.
# Everything the image needs is api/ and logs/ (minus their test-only
# files) and data/builds.
.git
.github
.superpowers
.worktrees
.ruff_cache
design
docs
research
web
data/pipeline
data/tests
data/diffs
data/curated
data/__pycache__
data/conftest.py
data/pyproject.toml
data/uv.lock
api/bin
api/docker-compose.test.yml
logs/bench
**/testdata
**/*.md
